{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianSumBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianSumBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gaussian.GaussianIntegral","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sum_exp_neg_mul_mul_pred_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sum_exp_neg_mul_mul_pred_le","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianSumBound.lean#L76-L99","doc":"The form a per-step tail bound produces: the penalty accumulated over `d`\nsteps is `1 + 2 + … + (d−1) = d(d−1)/2`, so the exponent carries `d(d−1)`, not\n`d²`.  Costs one extra unit because `d(d−1) ≥ (d−1)²` fails at `d = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sum_exp_neg_mul_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sum_exp_neg_mul_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianSumBound.lean#L54-L74","doc":"**The discrete Gaussian sum, bounded uniformly in the number of terms.**\n`∑_{d < m} e^{−a d²} ≤ 1 + ½√(π/a)`.  The `1` is the `d = 0` term, which the\nintegral comparison cannot see. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.integral_exp_neg_mul_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.integral_exp_neg_mul_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianSumBound.lean#L41-L52","doc":"`∫_0^M e^{−a x²} ≤ ½√(π/a)` — the half-line Gaussian dominates any\ninitial segment of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.antitoneOn_exp_neg_mul_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.antitoneOn_exp_neg_mul_sq","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianSumBound.lean#L32-L39","doc":"`x ↦ e^{−a x²}` is antitone on `[0, M]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}